From: postmarketOS Oculus Monterey maintainers <maintainers@postmarketos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: oculus: make 90 Hz the Lightman panel default

The production Quest 1 firmware running on Monterey exposes a 90 Hz panel
mode. Keep dynamic FPS enabled so the panel can use its 72 Hz compatibility
mode, but make 90 Hz the default and upper bound.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/oculus/dsi-panel-sdc-lightman-video.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/oculus/dsi-panel-sdc-lightman-video.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/oculus/dsi-panel-sdc-lightman-video.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/oculus/dsi-panel-sdc-lightman-video.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/oculus/dsi-panel-sdc-lightman-video.dtsi
@@ -31,2 +31,2 @@
-		qcom,mdss-dsi-max-refresh-rate = <72>;
-		qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-framerate = <72>;
+		qcom,mdss-dsi-max-refresh-rate = <90>;
+		qcom,mdss-dsi-panel-framerate = <90>;
